tion.dev","start":2305,"url":"https://t.co/gdKZXGN00h"},{"display_url":"t.co/V19R87wQid","end":2357,"expanded_url":"http://Motion.dev","start":2334,"url":"https://t.co/gdKZXGN00h"},{"display_url":"t.co/Jp9AReFaWe","end":2462,"expanded_url":"http://github.com/motiondivision/motion","start":2439,"url":"https://t.co/6f4sRazcLJ"},{"display_url":"t.co/TEG0FY4vFg","end":2575,"expanded_url":"http://github.com/airbnb/lottie-web","start":2552,"url":"https://t.co/40SBBUQFIt"}]},"text":"Give Opus 5.5 a motion design stack, not just a prompt.\n\n20 GitHub repos covering animation skills, sound, video rendering and interactive motion:\n\n*Skills + workflows*\n\n 1.⁠ ⁠claude-motion  \nMotion direction, frame checks and sound generated in code.  \n⁠ https://t.co/K5Asbqgztj ⁠\n\n 2.⁠ ⁠claude-motion-design  \nBuild videos with HTML, Playwright and FFmpeg. No Remotion.  \n⁠ https://t.co/0fnlHM1rcl ⁠\n\n 3.⁠ ⁠motion-graphics-skills  \n13 skills for creating product launch videos.  \n⁠ https://t.co/IaWH2KkXCd ⁠\n\n 4.⁠ ⁠claude-remotion-skill  \nA prompt-driven Remotion editor with captions, B-roll and sound.  \n⁠ https://t.co/rKb0U6Gq3E ⁠\n\n 5.⁠ ⁠klik-anim-skill-creation  \nAnimation principles and camera direction for Opus.  \n⁠ https://t.co/TDaoOMSOyG ⁠\n\n 6.⁠ ⁠hyperframes-motion-reel-skill  \nBuild a HyperFrames showreel synced to 120 BPM.  \n⁠ https://t.co/jlacxWXTME ⁠\n\n 7.⁠ ⁠product-launch-motion  \nLaunch films with voice-over, camera movement and color grading.  \n⁠ https://t.co/pbi5UvDnqg ⁠\n\n 8.⁠ ⁠animate  \nStoryboard and build a short animation in one canvas file.  \n⁠ https://t.co/WHYHq8qWsG ⁠\n\n 9.⁠ ⁠motion-design-skills  \nTiming, color, typography, logos and Remotion workflows.  \n⁠ https://t.co/OLSScRVA5O ⁠\n\n10.⁠ ⁠hyperframes-student-kit  \n14 skills and 406 motion graphics reference cards.  \n⁠ https://t.co/MNGGUfse94 ⁠\n\n*Rendering + animation engines*\n\n11.⁠ ⁠HyperFrames  \nTurn HTML animations into MP4 videos.  \n⁠ https://t.co/ZQYzJ0ER0U ⁠\n\n12.⁠ ⁠Remotion  \nCreate videos with React.  \n⁠ https://t.co/yngWME7mve ⁠\n\n13.⁠ ⁠Remotion Skills  \nOfficial Remotion skills for coding agents.  \n⁠ https://t.co/Yiy6g58CHN ⁠\n\n14.⁠ ⁠GSAP  \nAnimation timelines for controlling movement and transitions.  \n⁠ https://t.co/6xd7R1dihB ⁠\n\nInstall its skills:  \n⁠ npx skills add greensock/gsap-skills ⁠\n\n*Design principles + supporting tools*\n\n15.⁠ ⁠motion-design-skill  \nMotion principles that work across animation engines.  \n⁠ https://t.co/XBq4lAa2mA ⁠\n\n16.⁠ ⁠awesome-motion-design-agent-skills  \nA collection of GSAP, Remotion, Lottie and Rive skills.  \n⁠ https://t.co/RqFnO1Ygtd ⁠\n\n17.⁠ ⁠motion-graphics  \nGenerate B-roll from your transcript.  \n⁠ https://t.co/4FN4T59cZO ⁠\n\n18.⁠ ⁠motion-dev-animations-skill  \nWeb animations with https://t.co/gdKZXGN00h, not video exports.  \n⁠ https://t.co/354SNPd5tk ⁠\n\nhttps://t.co/gdKZXGN00h:  \n⁠ https://t.co/gdKZXGN00h ⁠\n\n19.⁠ ⁠Motion  \nThe web animation library formerly known as Framer Motion.  \n⁠ https://t.co/6f4sRazcLJ ⁠\n\n20.⁠ ⁠lottie-web  \nRender Lottie animations on the web instead of exporting MP4s.  \n⁠ https://t.co/40SBBUQFIt ⁠\n\nThe video workflow: Opus writes the code → skills guide the motion → an engine renders the result.\n\nCheck each repo before installing. Pick the tools your project actually needs."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":578,"impression_count":63197,"like_count":269,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":10,"retweet_count":28},"text":"Give Opus 5.5 a motion design stack, not just a prompt.\n\n20 GitHub repos covering animation skills, sound, video rendering and interactive motion:\n\n*Skills + workflows*\n\n 1.⁠ ⁠claude-motion  \nMotion direction, frame checks and sound generated in code.  \n⁠"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2108417784069681152"]},"author_id":"1435708926524284936","conversation_id":"2108417788352385181","created_at":"2026-10-09T04:42:27.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2108417788352385181"],"entiti